extends layout

block content
  article.about-page
    header.about-hero
      .about-container
        h1.about-title
          | Own a piece
          br
          | of the U.S. History.
        p.about-tagline Fake relics. Real political baggage.

    .about-container.about-content
      section.about-intro(aria-labelledby="about-intro-heading")
        .about-story
          h2#about-intro-heading.about-eyebrow About the Showroom

          p.about-lead History Showroom turns the objects behind America's most ridiculous political moments into fictional collectibles.

          p The laptop. The birth certificate. The ordinary object that somehow got its own news cycle. Think souvenirs from the stories you couldn't escape.

        p.about-stamp
          span National
          strong Distraction

      section.about-standards(aria-labelledby="about-standards-heading")
        h2#about-standards-heading The Collection

        dl.about-principles
          dt The inspiration
          dd Political spectacles, public meltdowns, and headlines that refused to die.

          dt The merchandise
          dd Made-up collectibles with unnecessarily detailed backstories.

          dt The appeal
          dd You had to hear about it. You might as well get a souvenir.

      section.about-team(aria-labelledby="about-team-heading")
        h2#about-team-heading Behind the Showroom

        p History Showroom was created as a student web development project.

        